  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is the current best at 0.591 acc, a large jump over singleprofile PCA (0.485), confirming multiprofile is a strong direction. Image-only is very weak (0.208), so the near-term gains likely come from refining the RNA pipeline. Question: Does transformer aggregation outperform avgpool for the same multiprofile PCA setup? config_003 changes only the aggregation (avgpool → transformer) while holding encoder and profile setting fixed, giving a clean single-variable comparison against the current best. Why this is the best use: With 6 experiments remaining, establishing whether transformer aggregation adds value over the simpler avgpool is the highest-information next step. If it helps, it unlocks a family of stronger multimodal configs (e.g., config_020/021); if it doesn't, we avoid wasting budget on transformer-based variants and can pivot to testing learned encoders (scvi/scgpt) or multimodal fusion instead."
